# Copy to frontend/.env.local for local development. Most setups need nothing
# here at all.
#
# By default the app calls /api/... on its own origin, which the Vite dev
# proxy (vite.config.ts) and the Vercel rewrite (vercel.json) forward to the
# backend. That keeps it same-origin, so there is no CORS preflight and no
# backend URL baked into the bundle.

# Point the dev proxy somewhere other than http://localhost:8000.
# VITE_DEV_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8001

# Escape hatch: call a backend cross-origin instead of going through the
# proxy. The backend must then list this app's origin in CORS_ORIGINS. Vite
# INLINES this at build time, so a deployed frontend must be rebuilt for a
# change to take effect.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://apex-backend-rouge.vercel.app
